WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:02.680
- [Narrator] This, true
believers, is a tale

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.460
where two storied parts of
American culture come together.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.670
It truly was a unicorn moment.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.140
Join us as we open the vault

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.692
of automobile and film history.

00:00:14.692 --> 00:00:17.745
(dramatic music)

00:00:17.745 --> 00:00:19.995
(coughing)

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.180
This is the story of Florence Lawrence.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.030
She was a full-blown star
of the silent film era.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:31.440
And, she's also the
inventor of the turn signal.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.340
Florence starred in over 300 films

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.373
produced by Biograph Studios.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.330
Her success led to a bit of wealth,

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.420
which she used to buy a car.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.070
A crazy expensive purchase at the time.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.550
It was love at first drive.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.870
Florence went from casual user

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.490
to automotive expert,

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.510
pursuing a knowledge
and expertise about cars

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.040
that outstripped even
her passion for acting.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.200
She invented features
to make driving safer

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.293
and more enjoyable.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.650
In 1914 she created a
signaling arm for cars

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.100
that would allow drivers to indicate

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.730
when they wanted to turn.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.050
Push a button, and her
invention raised a flag

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.360
on the bumper saying left or right.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.280
It was a great idea,
but sadly Florence never

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.060
registered her design.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.140
Versions of it popped up,
but it was another 10 years

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.240
before the turn signal was patented.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.530
And unfortunately, by somebody else.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.310
And that's when things
took a turn for the worse.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:28.640
She lost most of her wealth

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.080
in the stock market crash of 1929

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.280
and was injured in a fire on set.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.120
She never recovered her earlier success.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.170
Once the biggest movie star in the world,

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.600
now all but forgotten.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.490
But the fact remains: she was a pioneer

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:45.400
both as an actor and as a car enthusiast.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.060
And even as she fades from memory,

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:49.493
her contribution to cars remains.

00:01:49.493 --> 00:01:52.076
(gentle music)

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.363
(logo dinging)

